# PHP safety

## Required behavior

- Validate/normalize input at boundaries before business logic.
- Compare secrets with `hash_equals` when needed; use strong random (`random_bytes`).
- Path operations must reject traversal; never concatenate client filenames into filesystem paths.
- Output escaping belongs at the presentation boundary (CakePHP helpers/templates).
- Disable verbose error display in production; log instead.

## Anti-patterns

- Trusting client-side checks alone
- Building filesystem paths from raw user filenames
- Weak custom crypto for passwords
- Leaving `display_errors` on in production
